---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Legal Disclaimer"
  description="Reading the Law is an independent educational resource. This page explains what the site is, what it isn't, and the limits of the information provided."
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Disclaimer" />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <article class="prose-legal">
      <h2>Not legal advice</h2>
      <p>
        Reading the Law ("this site") provides general educational information about legal apprenticeship
        ("law office study" or "reading the law") programs in the United States. Nothing on this site
        constitutes legal advice, and using this site does not create an attorney-client relationship of
        any kind. You should not rely on this site as a substitute for advice from a licensed attorney or
        for guidance directly from the state bar admissions authority governing the jurisdiction you're
        interested in.
      </p>

      <h2>No affiliation with any state bar or admitting authority</h2>
      <p>
        This site is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated on behalf
        of the State Bar of California, the Vermont Board of Bar Examiners, the Virginia Board of Bar
        Examiners, the Washington State Bar Association, the Maine Board of Bar Examiners, the New York
        State Board of Law Examiners, or any other government body, court, or bar association.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and currency of information</h2>
      <p>
        We've made a good-faith effort to accurately summarize publicly available bar admission rules as of
        the date each page was last reviewed. Bar admission rules are set and amended by each state's
        governing authority and can change without notice. We do not guarantee that the information on this
        site is complete, current, or error-free. Before making any decision (including committing years of
        your life to a program described here), confirm current requirements directly with the official
        governing body listed on the relevant page.
      </p>

      <h2>Outcomes are not guaranteed</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site guarantees that you will be admitted to any program, pass any interim
        examination, complete any course of study, pass any bar examination, or be admitted to practice
        law. Statistics referenced on this site (such as bar passage rates) are general and historical in
        nature and are not a prediction of any individual's results.
      </p>

      <h2>Future matchmaking platform</h2>
      <p>
        The matchmaking platform described on this site is in development and is not yet operational. Any
        waitlist signup is solely for the purpose of contacting you when and if the platform becomes
        available, and does not create any obligation on our part or any right on yours to access the
        platform on any particular timeline.
      </p>

      <h2>External links</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to official government and bar association websites for verification purposes. We
        don't control those sites' content and aren't responsible for their accuracy or availability.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        If you notice information on this site that appears outdated or incorrect, we want to know. Email
        us at <a href="mailto:readingthelaw@gmail.com">readingthelaw@gmail.com</a> or reach out through the
        waitlist form on the <a href="/matchmaking/">matchmaking page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
